OFFICIAL-SENSITIVE

Cumbria LRF - Storm Fenella response - SITREP 5
Time of report: 14/01/2026 1800

1. SITUATION
Incident status: Active response
Further heavy rain expected overnight on high ground.

2. SITES AND ROUTES
- the Pooley Bridge crossing: closed as a precaution
- Northside Bridge: closed to all traffic
- A66 west of Penrith: open with restrictions
- West Coast Main Line: CLOSED
- A591 near Thirlmere: closed - flooding
- Riverside Community Centre: operating as a rest centre (run by Cumberland Council)
- Cockermouth School: operating as a rest centre
- Glenridding Village Hall: rest centre OPEN (run by W&F Council)
- Fellside Care Home: EVACUATED (run by Fellside Care Ltd)
- Queen Elizabeth School: closed to pupils
- Keswick School: rest centre OPEN (run by Cumberland Council EP team)
- junction 40 of the M6: open with restrictions (run by Highways England)

3. AGENCIES RESPONDING
British Red Cross, North West Ambluance Service, National Highways, ENW, Westmorland & Furness Council, North Cumbria Integrated Care NHS Foundation Trust

4. NEXT MEETING
SCG at 1800. Dial-in details as previously circulated.

